----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRING-=====>

1->
String- String is an array of character ending or terminated with null character ('\0').
Syntax:
char array_name[size];

2->
Input function.
- scanf("%s",string_var);- it is not capable of accepeting multiword string.
- scanf("%[^\n]s",string_var);- it is capable of accepeting multiword string.
- gets(string_var);- it is capable of accepeting multiword string.

3->
Output function.
- printf("%s",string_var);
- puts(string_var);

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRING LIBRARY FUNCTION-=>

1->
String concatenation- Process of joining two strings.
Syntax:
strcat(string1,string2);

2->
String comparison- Process of compare two strings.
Syntax:
strcmp(string1,string2);

strcmp(string1,string2);
<0 when string1 < string2
=0 when string1 = string2
>0 when string1 > string2

3->
String copying- Process of copying one string into other strings.
Syntax:
strcpy(string1,string2);

4->
String length- Process of knowing no of character of strings.
Syntax:
strlen(string);

5->
String reverse- Process of exchange the character of strings-->>
Syntax:
strrev(string);

